TITLE:: MidiToScAdapter
SUMMARY:: Allows a SynthDef to be played via MIDI.
CATEGORIES:: External Control
RELATED:: Classes/Tuner

DESCRIPTION::
Sets up LINK::Classes/MIDIdef::s to play a LINK::Classes/SynthDef::, creating and destroying LINK::Classes/Synth:: instances in response to the incoming note on and note off messages.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new instance of TELETYPE::MidiToScAdapter::.

ARGUMENT:: synthDefName
A LINK::Classes/Symbol:: which is the name of the LINK::Classes/SynthDef:: to be played.

ARGUMENT:: midiChannel
An optional LINK::Classes/Integer:: specifying which MIDI channel should play the LINK::Classes/SynthDef::. If not specified, all MIDI channels will play the LINK::Classes/SynthDef::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: free
Frees all resources associated with the TELETYPE::MidiToScAdapter::, including any running LINK::Classes/Synth:: instances.

METHOD:: set
Allows parameters on any playing LINK::Classes/Synth:: instances to be set.

ARGUMENT:: ... parameters
The same as the parameters provided to LINK::Classes/Node#-set::, i.e. alternating keys and values.

PRIVATE::init

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
~foo = MidiToScAdapter(\default, 8);
// Now noodle on the keyboard
~foo.set(\amp,0); // Should silence any active instances (although they are still playing)
// Noodle a bit more
~foo.free;
::